{"key":"enterprise/T1199","id":"T1199","name":"Trusted Relationship","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["initial-access"],"platforms":["IaaS","Identity Provider","Linux","macOS","Office Suite","SaaS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","identity","onprem","saas"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may breach or otherwise leverage organizations who have access to intended victims. Access through trusted third party relationship abuses an existing connection that may not be protected or receives less scrutiny than standard mechanisms of gaining access to a network. Organizations often grant elevated access to second or third-party external providers in order to allow them to manage internal systems as well as cloud-based…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1199","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--9fa07bef-9c81-421e-a8e5-ad4366c5a925","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.706Z","source_object_version":"2.4","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0038","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9c2fa0ae-7abc-485a-97f6-699e3b6cf9fa","page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"id":"DC0067","name":"Logon Session Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0067","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9ce98c86-8d30-4043-ba54-0784d478d0b5","page":"telemetry/DC0067/"},{"id":"DC0088","name":"Logon Session Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0088","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--39b9db72-8b48-4595-a18d-db5bbba3091b","page":"telemetry/DC0088/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0488","name":"Detect abuse of Trusted Relationships (third-party and delegated admin access)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--2f7a5ebd-e025-4822-aed2-46fc3ec1a0a9","relationship_id":"relationship--8dcb3689-54f5-4416-9b75-6c380d24bdca"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1344","name":"Analytic 1344","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488#AN1344","guidance":"Behavioral chain: (1) a login from a third-party account or untrusted source network establishes an interactive/remote session; (2) the session acquires elevated privileges or accesses sensitive resources atypical for that account; (3) subsequent lateral movement or data access occurs from the same session/device. Correlate Windows logon events, token elevation/privileged use, and resource access with third-party context.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0488"},{"id":"AN1345","name":"Analytic 1345","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488#AN1345","guidance":"Behavioral chain: (1) sshd or federated SSO logins from third-party networks or identities; (2) rapid sudo/su privilege elevation; (3) access to sensitive paths or east-west SSH. Correlate auth logs, process execution, and network flows.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0488"},{"id":"AN1346","name":"Analytic 1346","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488#AN1346","guidance":"Behavioral chain: (1) third-party interactive login or mobileconfig-based device enrollment; (2) privilege use or admin group change; (3) lateral movement mounts/ssh. Correlate unified logs and network telemetry.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0488"},{"id":"AN1347","name":"Analytic 1347","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488#AN1347","guidance":"Behavioral chain: (1) delegated admin or external identity establishes session (e.g., partner/reseller DAP, B2B guest, SAML/OAuth trust); (2) role elevation or app consent/permission grant; (3) downstream privileged actions in the tenant. Correlate IdP sign-in, admin/role assignment, and consent/admin-on-behalf events.","platforms":["Identity Provider"],"strategy_id":"DET0488"},{"id":"AN1348","name":"Analytic 1348","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488#AN1348","guidance":"Behavioral chain: (1) cross-account or third-party principal assumes a role into the tenant/subscription/project; (2) privileged API calls are made in short succession; (3) access originates from unfamiliar networks or geos. Correlate assume-role/federation events with sensitive API usage.","platforms":["IaaS"],"strategy_id":"DET0488"},{"id":"AN1349","name":"Analytic 1349","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488#AN1349","guidance":"Behavioral chain: (1) third-party app or admin connects via OAuth/marketplace install; (2) high-privilege scopes granted; (3) anomalous actions (mass read/exports, admin changes).","platforms":["SaaS"],"strategy_id":"DET0488"},{"id":"AN1350","name":"Analytic 1350","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488#AN1350","guidance":"Behavioral chain: (1) delegated administration offers/relationships created or modified by partner tenants; (2) mailbox delegation/impersonation enabled; (3) follow-on access from partner IPs.","platforms":["Office Suite"],"strategy_id":"DET0488"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0067","component":"Logon Session Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4624, 4648","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1344","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0488#AN1344","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0067/"},{"component_id":"DC0088","component":"Logon Session Metadata","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4776, 4771, 4770","platforms":["